Subject: [PATCH] wave: declare unavailable native data TX status

The BSS ring reports management and NULL-frame ACKs. The ordinary Ethernet
data completion only releases buffer ownership. Preserve the former's MLME
feedback while excluding incomplete mac80211 retry/failure defaults from
native station statistics.

Requires the mac80211 NO_DATA_TX_STATUS capability contract.

--- a/wireless/driver/linux/mac80211.c
+++ b/wireless/driver/linux/mac80211.c
@@ -2404,6 +2404,10 @@
   ieee80211_hw_set(hw, KEY_REPLACE_IN_PLACE);
   ieee80211_hw_set(hw, AMPDU_AGGREGATION);
 #endif
+  /* BSS completions report management/NULL ACKs. Ordinary Ethernet data
+   * completions only return buffer ownership; their retry/failure totals
+   * cannot be supplied by mac80211's management-only status counters. */
+  ieee80211_hw_set(hw, NO_DATA_TX_STATUS);
 
   /* Driver's private station information */
   hw->sta_data_size = 0;
